  "notes": "Cash basis village. Governmental = General (incl. Library, combined in statement) and Street funds, Total Governmental Funds column p5. Business-type = Sanitation and Water and Sewer, Total Proprietary Funds column p7; measure cash; bond proceeds 180,000 recorded in business_type.debt_proceeds, not receipts; business-type receipts/disbursements have no single printed total so totals computed (operating + nonoperating; disbursements agree with p2 384,811). Governmental roll-forward: 342,074 + 401,546 - 404,359 + 32,782 - 35,218 + 35,000 = 371,825. Balance sheet = government-wide Statement of Net Position - Cash Basis, Total column (p1). Detail: p9-10 schedule by fund (actual only, no budget column) recorded for each fund; zero-amount lines omitted. The p8 All Funds budgetary comparison (budget and actual, combined funds; actual taxes 80,645, local 292,626, etc.) not recorded to avoid double counting with the per-fund schedule; no per-fund budget figures are printed. The p9 General fund schedule includes Library fund as separate column; statement p5 combines them. Transfer cross-check: schedule transfers in 49,109 = out 49,109. General out 47,270 includes 12,052 to Library (internal, eliminated in p5 statement: 47,270 - 12,052 = 35,218 out). Statement governmental out 35,218 = 30,943 to Street + 4,275 to Water and Sewer; in 32,782 = 1,839 from Sanitation to General + 30,943 to Street. Business-type net transfers +2,436 offsets governmental net -2,436. All match; no hidden transfers inside spending lines found. Local receipts line (89,414) is a mix of fees, grants and misc per pp2-3 but is not itself broken down, so kept as one line. Read pages 1-10 of 10 Statement line Local 89,414 split by the Statement of Activities (pp2-3) into fees 64,595, operating grants and contributions 17,347 and miscellaneous 7,472 (ties exactly)."
